		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Gene unlock tree\n\nEach arrow runs from a gene to the gene it unlocks. The source is the **Genetic Prerequisites** line on the target note.\n\nGreen **unlocks** — that parent is the only genetic prerequisite.\nCyan **required** — that parent is mandatory, and the target also needs one orange parent.\nOrange **one of** — any single orange parent satisfies that part of the gate.","x":80,"y":-420,"width":980,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"### How to read a gate\n\n**Glycon Synthase** — Carbex Permease, plus Reducin Dehydrogenase or Reaction Center.\n**Photochrome** — any one pigment synthase (Rhodin, Chlorin, Carotin, or Phycin).\n**Taxis Regulator** — Flagellar Motor Protein, plus any one receptor.\n**Plasmid Maintainer** — Conjugation Apparatus or Competence Uptake.\n\nRhodopsin phototrophy and chlorophyll phototrophy are separate lineages.\nCard colors follow the catalog: green metabolism, orange homeostasis, cyan motility, yellow perception, purple regulation, red reproduction.","x":1100,"y":-420,"width":860,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ATPS","type":"file","file":"Genes/ATP Synthase (ATPS).md","x":80,"y":40,"width":400,"height":52,"color":"4"},
